{
 "about": "Post records (appendix A 19-21, 33). parser post: one raw X tweet result (as found at tweet_results.result) to one record. expected lists only the fields the case is about; a field not named is free. Field names are the skill's own, shared with the threads skill where the concept is the same (author, text, like_count, repost_count, reply_to_id, root_post_id, quoted_post, reposted_post, is_pinned, unavailable); X-only ideas keep X's meaning (view_count, bookmark_count, is_long_post, limited_actions). A post's own URL is https://x.com/<author handle>/status/<id>, or /i/web/status/<id> when X sent no author. Counts X did not send are null. Times are UTC ISO. source: code (previous records.py), plan (a decided change), P2 (shape not yet seen live; the case is a placeholder until the recon captures fix it). All people, ids and links are synthetic.",
 "users": {
  "A": {
   "__typename": "User",
   "rest_id": "1000000001",
   "core": {
    "screen_name": "example_author",
    "name": "Example Author"
   },
   "legacy": {}
  },
  "B": {
   "__typename": "User",
   "rest_id": "1000000002",
   "core": {
    "screen_name": "second_person",
    "name": "Second Person"
   },
   "legacy": {}
  },
  "C": {
   "__typename": "User",
   "rest_id": "1000000003",
   "core": {
    "screen_name": "third_person",
    "name": "Third Person"
   },
   "legacy": {}
  }
 },
